Relevant columns and potential usage
• PATENTS.PATENTS.PUBLICATIONS."cpc": CPC classification codes (filter to A01B3%).  
• PATENTS.PATENTS.PUBLICATIONS."assignee_harmonized": assignee names (count applications per assignee).  
• PATENTS.PATENTS.PUBLICATIONS."publication_number": unique ID for each application / publication (to be counted).  
• PATENTS.PATENTS.PUBLICATIONS."publication_date": yyyymmdd numeric; extract the year to find the busiest year for each assignee.  
• PATENTS.PATENTS.PUBLICATIONS."country_code": country of the publication; find most‑frequent country in the peak year.  
• PATENTS.PATENTS.CPC_DEFINITION."symbol", "titleFull": vocabulary/definition table – verify the CPC symbols that start with ‘A01B3’.

Basic conditions that will be used
1. Flatten the VARIANT arrays (“cpc”, “assignee_harmonized”).  
2. f.value:"symbol"::STRING ILIKE 'A01B3%' –– keep only CPC symbols that begin with A01B3.  
3. Extract year with ( "publication_date" / 10000 )::INT  (avoid date functions).  

Exploratory SQLs (10 queries, each limited to 20 rows)

